Contains Duplicate ⭐

Determine whether an array contains any value more than once.

Input:  [1, 2, 3, 1]
Output: true

Input:  [1, 2, 3, 4]
Output: false


Solution:


const num = [1, 2, 3, 1];
let set = new Set();
let containsDuplicate = false;

for (let i = 0; i < num.length; i++) {
  if (set.has(num[i])) {
    containsDuplicate = true;
    break;
  }
  set.add(num[i]);
}

console.log(containsDuplicate);
